Assuming every call to fork() succeeds, how many times is "Hi" printed by the program below?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>

int main(void) {
    fork();
    fork();
    fork();
    printf("Hi\n");
    return 0;
}
```

Binary semaphores S and Q are both initialised to 1. Two processes run concurrently:

```
P1:                 P2:
wait(S);            wait(Q);
wait(Q);            wait(S);
/* critical */      /* critical */
signal(Q);          signal(S);
signal(S);          signal(Q);
```

Which statement is correct?

Binary semaphores S1 = 1 and S2 = 0. Two processes run concurrently forever:

```
Process X:          Process Y:
while (true) {      while (true) {
    wait(S1);           wait(S2);
    print("0");         print("1");
    signal(S2);         signal(S1);
}                   }
```

Which output is guaranteed?
